WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.190
The culture festival is finally drawing near...

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.270
...so our days have been filled with nothing but preparations.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.030
Yano, where are you?

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.030
Hey, have you seen Yano?

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.530
Ah, Yano? I think he's around here somewhere, so I'll take a look.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.090
Are you sure that's really all right?

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.130
Yeah.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.380
One thing I'm especially good at...

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.430
That's amazing.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.090
Really?

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.640
...is finding Yano, whenever or wherever he may be.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.310
Yano.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.060
Because he's the one I love.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.200
He's the one I love.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.250
But...

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.040
Do you have your lines down pat?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.500
Yeah, I guess.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:44.140
Is it just my imagination, or has he seemed distant lately?

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.480
He's been like this ever since the day we had those steamed meat buns...

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.480
Oh, Yano.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.440
What's up?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.350
You see...

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.110
A happy dream?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:54.940
Yeah.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.660
What's happiness...?

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.870
I wonder what it is?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:03.910
That's a tough one.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.580
Umm...

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.830
Uhh...

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.120
Ah! Something warm.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:11.920
Something warm?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.540
Yeah! Like a steamed meat bun or a roasted sweet potato.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.130
Something that warms you up on a cold day.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.050
Something that soothes your heart.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.130
A steamed meat bun, huh?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.140
Well, it can be anything, like a book you like or a CD.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.640
Or someone you like.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.730
Let's go get some steamed meat buns.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.030
Nana, that ring's really cute.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.200
Huh? Ah, this?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.000
Yeah! It's adorable!

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.250
Thanks.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.500
It's glass, though.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.300
Who did you force into buying that for you? Really!

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.510
I bought it myself.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.140
Buying a ring for yourself... is pretty sad, isn't it?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.140
Yeah.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.010
Really?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.560
Ah, sorry!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.480
Geez! I can't believe this!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.360
It's running. What are we gonna do about this?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.690
Ah... that really sucks.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.570
That'll have to be completely redrawn.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.860
You're so mean.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.740
After it was looking so good, too...

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.030
We're out of time now. What are we gonna do?

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.990
We're going to have to buy new paper.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.410
Unless we have any leftover...

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.580
Should I help out?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.840
Huh? You don't mind?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.430
Nope. I'm free right now, and it's just some painting, right?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.340
Thanks a ton!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.720
Yano's pretty nice.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.350
How unusual...

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.350
Yamamoto-san, could you get a brush for Yano?

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:04.530
You're always slacking off, and you only pretend to be helpful at times like these.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.030
You're pretty good at that, aren't you?

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.290
I... I don't think so.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.420
After all, since he's the lead in the play, he must be having the toughest time.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.590
It's true that he's skipped a lot of rehearsals, but he also memorizes his lines quickly...

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.510
...so he's getting done what needs to be done.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.310
Takahashi-san, you're too easy on Yano.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.190
This is kind of weird, don't you think?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.770
Whenever anyone says anything to Yano...

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.400
...he avoids the question or shuts them up. It's always one or the other.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.780
But when Yamamoto-san said that stuff to him, he didn't respond at all.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.700
Isn't that weird?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.250
Do you think it could be because of that?

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.910
She's Nana-san's little sister.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:56.960
There's history between them.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.920
Nana-san...

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.970
...was the girl Yano was going out with in middle school.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.470
But last year, she died in a car accident.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.600
That's what I don't get!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.350
What's the big deal? She's just the little sister!

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.310
It's not like it was Yano's fault her older sister died.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.060
He should be the one blaming other people!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.860
Not only did she betray him, but then she went and died!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.110
Really, Yano should be the one holding a grudge, not Yamamoto-san!

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.110
Now, now. Mizu-chan, calm down.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.870
I wonder if I'm really that soft with Yano...

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.660
Huh? Don't you act the same as anyone else?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.540
Yamamoto-san's the one who's a little weird. Definitely.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.380
Yamamoto-san... might have liked Yano.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.840
Ah, I could see that!

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.600
And she resents him for turning her down.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:00.730
I... don't think Yamamoto-san's like that.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:04.940
Ah... maybe. She doesn't seem that simple.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:10.700
I'm not a big fan of her myself, but I do think she's a pretty reasonable person.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:18.200
That's why I think Yano always restrains himself around Yamamoto-san.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.540
It's like he has some hidden reason he feels guilty about.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.440
Yano.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.740
Sorry about earlier.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.240
Huh? For what?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.160
You seemed like you couldn't really respond to Yamamoto-san, so I...

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.950
Ah, I really didn't care.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.410
Take!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.540
You heading home?

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.290
Yeah, in a bit.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.410
Let's stop by the plaza on the way.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.210
There's a long-sleeved T-shirt I really wanna get.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.040
How many T-shirts do you need before you're satisfied?

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.300
Well, excuse me for buying so many.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.300
You're so bizarre.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.550
That I am.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.260
Ah, Takahashi.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.890
Yes?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.610
You don't have to be so protective of me like before. It's unnecessary.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.030
I... I guess.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:36.160
But I really thought you were doing your best...

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.120
And I'm telling you, you don't need to say that sort of stuff.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.500
I... I guess you're right...

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:53.840
I'm sorry I stuck my nose into your business.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:54.840
Sorry.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.900
Let's go.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.990
Why are you so mean to her?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.280
I don't think I am... I'm just being me.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.080
Then, why don't you try being kinder?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.420
Why do I have to?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:28.920
You're weird.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:35.550
Whenever she's around I can't concentrate.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.340
Did you say something just now?

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.800
Never mind.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:52.110
My name is Kohsaka, and I'm in charge of producing this class's short play.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.570
"The Peak of Hope".

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.700
This story is a masterpiece that will make anyone and everyone cry.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.530
And with the culture festival right before our eyes, the rehearsals should be coming to a close.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:04.120
After all, the real thing's happening the day after tomorrow.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.540
"Don't you think we've had enough rehearsals?"

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.620
"Let's hurry and get the real thing over with!"

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.460
...are some of the things I should be hearing in these final preparations.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.550
But!

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.720
It's actually nothing like that right now!

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.340
And that's because...!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.550
Yano-kun, you skipped too many rehearsals.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.340
This isn't a laughing matter.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.970
All right. Let's do this, Yano!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:23.850
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.730
Will Yano really be all right?

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.640
It doesn't look like he has a drop of motivation in him.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.110
Didn't someone say he always gets things done when they need to get done?

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.110
We have no choice but to put our faith in that, huh, Nana?

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.860
Y-Yeah...

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.120
I won't say anything... I won't say anything unnecessary.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.410
Okay! Starting from the scene on page 25!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:52.960
Drawing your sword on someone holding a mere hoe... I can see how the mighty warriors have fallen.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.800
I can't say anything untoward, but drop your weapon, and do as I say.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.510
Otherwise, I cannot guarantee your life.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.010
Cut!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.390
What's with that reading?!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.350
Put more feeling into it! Feeling!

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:08.600
Umm... I don't really want to ask, but don't you have your lines memorized?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.770
Well, there are so many long scenes.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.610
The real thing's the day after tomorrow!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:14.520
Get someone to hold up cue cards during the real thing.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:15.780
That's impossible!

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.280
It is?

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.110
Memorize your lines!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:20.070
He doesn't take care of things when they need to get done at all...

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.160
Will we really be all right in time for the actual show?

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.830
Nana, say something to him.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.830
You're the class president, right?

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:30.870
B-But that and this don't really have much to do with each other.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.790
And I'm busy enough with my own role...

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:38.380
Yano, please! It's the day after tomorrow!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.930
By the day after tomorrow, cram as many lines as you can into your head!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.220
I'll be sure to have it perfect. Perfect, perfect.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.470
I'm being serious here!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.470
Ah... my stomach's starting to hurt.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.530
Hey, how do you read this?

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.660
Mount Kyokurin? Mount Kokurin?

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.700
You're still only at that low level?

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.290
He turned away from me...

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.010
You don't have to be so protective of me like before. It's unnecessary.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.510
Let's go get some steamed meat buns.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.720
Nana-chan.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.010
Y-Yes?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.770
Let me borrow your chest.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:38.980
I don't understand...

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:43.910
I don't...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.620
...understand Yano.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.850
I don't understand...

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.810
I just don't understand.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.560
I wonder if we won't...

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.530
...be able to talk like we did before...

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.500
Today, I heard a strange tale from a monk travelling the countryside.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:42.210
He spoke of a golden lichen growing upon the peak of Mount Kyokurin...

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.470
...so holy that if one were to sow it elsewhere...

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.970
...it would transform a wasteland into a land of abundant harvest...

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.220
...and all quarrels between people would vanish, and peace would flourish everywhere.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:56.600
And because of this, people have called that peak upon Mount Kyokurin the "Peak of Hope".

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.730
Yano can really be amazing at times...

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.690
Yano, that was wonderful! Your acting was spectacular!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.150
Don't cry over it.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.740
Thank you! Thank you!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:09.450
You're amazing... I want to tell Yano that he's amazing...

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:12.410
But...

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.790
I should be memorizing my lines right now! I have to get all three down! All three!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:20.540
Nana...

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.750
I see you're still as easy as ever...

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:32.810
There's a huge crowd!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.140
Yano's fame really is incredible!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.480
I hope this goes off well, Nana.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.400
She's still reading the script...

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.940
Where is Yano, anyway?

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.570
Ah, he's changing right now.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:44.860
He's always doing things last minute...

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.990
I'm not sure whether to call it airheadedness or what...

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.870
Even though I'm just Village Girl #2 and I only have three lines...

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.530
...I wish he'd share some of his courage... sheesh.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.740
Ah, Yano!

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:06.300
I... won't say anything.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.720
Why are there so many people here?

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.680
What do you mean? They're all here to see you!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.770
Now, Yano-kun, we're counting on you today.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.310
What was my first line again...?

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.690
Crap... I might've forgotten all my lines.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.900
F-First, calm down!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.320
Take deep breaths! Deep breaths!

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.690
Just picture yourself doing it correctly!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:27.440
Have some water!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.150
The script, the script!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.490
He doesn't have to read it! Yano will do just fine!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.290
Right, Yano?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:41.460
Yeah.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:42.670
All right!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.670
Okay, you're almost up.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.420
Yeah! You're on standby!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.630
Yano-kun, go for it.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:53.640
I said something unnecessary again...

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.600
Br...

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.810
Break a leg.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.500
Umm... there's something on that mountain over there. Er, what was it called again?

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.500
D-Do you mean Mount Kyokurin?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.010
Ah, yeah! That one, that one.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.880
It's supposed to have this so-called... Umm... what was it again?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:32.550
The something-or-other peak.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.680
It's the Peak of Hope!

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:35.890
They like it...

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.930
Amazing...

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.970
Even though all of his lines are random...

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.390
The audience hasn't realized.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.440
He has such a way with words...

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.310
And that complete lack of stage fright...

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.650
He's strong in these serious events.

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.980
It's such a pain, though...

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.360
P-Please! We beg of you!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.360
You don't have to be so protective of me like before.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.870
I was actually really happy.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.750
...was the mistake you're making it out to be.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:05.750
I don't know which is the real Yano...

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.510
You're up.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.260
Sir Samurai, please calm down!

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.480
I guess I will! If I were as out of hand as you, I'd fall over!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:40.830
Or could it be that they're all the real him?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.790
All right! All right!

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:50.290
It was a huge success, huh?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.590
But anyway, this is really heavy!

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.890
So this is how it ends, huh?

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.600
Nothing really happened...

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.100
Coming through!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.020
What's the matter, Nana?

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.730
The top of my ring came off!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.570
Ah, the one you bought for yourself?

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.570
Nana, just give up on it.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.660
It'll be impossible to find.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.750
I liked it, too...

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.330
Ow.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.040
What are you do--

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:32.090
Weird ring.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.090
He surprised me...

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.430
Die, you jerk.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.800
A person shouldn't go around telling people to "die" all the time.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:41.930
Why's that?

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.430
If I were to actually die tomorrow in a car accident or something...

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.850
...you'd feel bad, even though it wouldn't have been your fault, right?

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.690
As if something convenient like that would--

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.070
Did you tell her that...?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.150
I'm not you.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.700
So I don't say things like that!

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.070
I'm different from the savage Takahashi!

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.490
In the first place, saying "die" is so boringly simple.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.000
Boringly simple?

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:07.830
Okay. Then how about, "I'll kill you, bitch"?

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.540
Takahashi's of low character!

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:16.670
Before I knew it, we were speaking normally...

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:19.760
Don't you think dying's such an easy way out?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.340
Then, what would you do?

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.810
First, I'd break a person's fingers one by one...

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:26.270
...then pull each of his nails...

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:27.390
You don't have to keep going...

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.940
Let's just agree that you're a sadist.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.150
That's not what I meant, anyway.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:32.400
It's not that...

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.280
It's just that when you die, you don't feel anything or know what happened.

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.530
Isn't that too boring?

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.150
Umm...

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:50.000
It always feels like I'm about to understand him, but then he gets away...

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.800
Love confession time!

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.680
I hear that during things like this, couples step forward and dance cheek-to-cheek!

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:01.840
Oh, stop it!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.390
I wonder if someone's confessing to Yano right now...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.610
I'm especially good at...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.250
Could you imagine if someone confessed to you?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.080
Where are you?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.500
Takahashi.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.010
I'll give you something nice.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.220
Ah, whoops. Wrong thing.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.970
It's yours, right?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.730
Let me fix it for you.

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:54.480
Even if the ring's weird, I still feel kinda bad for it.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:03.740
He's so cute...

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.740
Hold out your right hand.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.740
It won't fit!

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:08.660
You've put on weight, haven't you?

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.200
It doesn't go on my thumb!

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.450
Then, on this finger.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:18.420
It's like we're exchanging wedding rings...

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.670
The words they say at weddings sure are nice, huh?

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:26.970
"Do you take this woman to be your wife, and vow to love her forever?"

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:30.310
I do!

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.520
Are we getting married out here?

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.020
I-It just slipped out.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.520
Don't laugh, moron.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.360
B-But words aren't good enough!

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.530
If I were in that situation, I'd probably say something like this...

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.950
Please break my fingers.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.880
What are you saying?

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:02.510
You're crazy. Crazy!

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:10.470
Takahashi.

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.900
I'll only say this once, so listen carefully.

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.530
I love you.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:30.910
No way...

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:47.880
Takahashi...

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:27.510
Far in the distance, I heard the sound of fireworks...
